1. Valuation of Assets
All assets of a life insurer shall be valued in accordance with Schedule- II - Finance functions of these
regulations, other applicable Regulations, including IRDAI (Registration, Capital Structure, Transfer of
Shares and Amalgamation of Insurers) Regulations, 2024 and applicable extant norms, except the
following assets which shall be placed with value zero for solvency margin computation:
(1) Agents' and Intermediaries' balances and outstanding premiums in India, to the extent they are not
realised within a period of thirty days;
(2) Agents' and Intermediaries' balances and outstanding premiums outside India, to the extent they are
not realisable;
(3) Sundry debts, to the extent they are not realisable;
